#
# Architecture-neutral IO syscall policy layer. Syscall numbers, the raw syscall
# instruction, byte-level memory primitives, and the legacy/at operation shims
# all live in the per-architecture modules selected by the compiler's "native"
# arch token (uranite.os.arch.native.*). This module keeps the portable pieces:
# the Linux flag/errno/stat constants, errno-to-error mapping, and the thin sysX
# wrappers that check SyscallResult and raise the appropriate IOError subclass.
#
